WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.800
Missing logs leave teams unable to reconstruct important events.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.180
Payment applications should capture authentication, authorization failures,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.960
administrative actions, sensitive data access, transaction changes,

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.020
and configuration changes.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.400
Poor alerting creates noise without action or misses the events that matter most.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.020
Alerts should focus on suspicious behavior, high-risk changes, fraud indicators,

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.600
and activity affecting the cardholder data environment.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.540
Delayed detection increases the time attackers have to abuse accounts, alter transactions,

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:38.520
move laterally, or destroy evidence. Monitoring needs clear ownership and response paths.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.540
Insufficient monitoring can also harm assessment readiness.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.880
PCI DSS expects audit trails and review processes that support investigation,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.900
accountability, and security operations.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.680
Centralize application, identity, infrastructure, and cloud logs.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.500
Integrate security telemetry with SIEM or monitoring workflows.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.880
Review logs and alerts through documented, repeatable processes.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:09.180
Selected PCI DSS mappings for this topic include Req. 10.2 - Audit logs; Req.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:15.480
10.4 - Log review; Req. 10.6 - Daily log review processes.
